; A higher-order helper that takes an array of functions and RETURNS a
; closure, and is never called from anywhere. Its mere presence once crashed
; audio-mode bytecode compilation.
;
; An `@audio` entry triggers eager compilation of the whole program's audio
; source. Unlike the WGSL/C backends' closure-based emission — and unlike
; CPU-mode compilation — audio mode used to compile every non-CPU-exclusive
; function whether or not it was reachable from an audio entry. Compiling
; this unreachable helper reached its returned closure `(fn [pos] pos)` —
; extracted to a top-level function that audio-mode discovery never added to
; the compiled set — and aborted with "Name ... not found in scope".
;
; Audio mode now reachability-filters from its own `@audio` entries (like the
; CPU runtime filters from `@cpu` entries), so an unreachable helper is never
; compiled. Both runtimes must compile and run this.
(defn merge-distortion-layers
  [layers: [(Fn [vec3f] vec3f)]]: (Fn [vec3f] vec3f)
  (fn [pos] pos))

@audio
(defn tone [t: f32]: f32
  (sin (* 440. t)))

@cpu
(defn main []
  (print 1u))
